jb — a minimal agentic coding loop
==================================

jb reads a prompt from standard input, sends it to a language model
API, executes tool calls in a loop, and prints the final answer to
standard output.  Single C binary, zero runtime dependencies except
curl(1) and POSIX.

Building:

    make

Installing:

    make install          # PREFIX=/usr/local
    make install PREFIX=~ # install to ~/bin and ~/.local/share/man/man1

Configuration lives in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jb/config.json.  You need an
API key in JB_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY.  See jb(1) for full
documentation.

